---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { originStory } from "../../data/field-notes";
---
<BaseLayout title="Dean Lofts" description="Dean Lofts builds systems that turn intent into shipped software, then builds controls around what reality proves was wrong." path="/dean/" image="/og/dean.jpg">
  <script
    slot="head"
    type="application/ld+json"
    set:html={JSON.stringify({
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "Person",
      name: "Dean Lofts",
      url: "https://woodhouse.loftwah.com/dean/",
      sameAs: ["https://github.com/loftwah", "https://x.com/loftwah", "https://au.linkedin.com/in/deanlofts"]
    })}
  />
  <section class="container dossier-hero">
    <div>
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">WOODHOUSE</a><span>/</span><span>Dean</span></nav>
      <p class="eyebrow">The human operator</p>
      <h1>Dean Lofts.</h1>
      <p class="dossier-hero__summary">{originStory.close}</p>
    </div>
    <aside class="dossier-hero__side"><span class="micro-label">Systems · platform · products · agents</span><dl><dt>Based</dt><dd>Melbourne, Australia</dd><dt>Working on</dt><dd>The Loftwah Software Factory</dd></dl></aside>
  </section>
  <section class="container dossier-grid">
    <article class="prose">
      <h2>How the work got here</h2>
      <p>{originStory.introduction}</p>
      {originStory.body.map((paragraph) => <p>{paragraph}</p>)}
      <h2>What I build</h2>
      <p>Systems that move an idea toward a running product: applications, infrastructure, release paths, agent workflows and the controls that keep their claims honest.</p>
      <p>The projects are varied on purpose. Games expose product and visual judgement. Media systems expose catalog, playback and delivery. Reconstruction work tests whether an agent can stay inside source evidence. MAX tests where software proof stops and physical proof begins.</p>
      <h2>The work should carry the résumé</h2>
      <p>Woodhouse is a public record of the products, their architecture and the factory lessons that survive. It is not a list of unsupported adjectives. Start with the <a href="/factory/">projects</a>, then follow the <a href="/incidents/">incidents</a> and <a href="/architecture/">architecture</a>.</p>
    </article>
    <aside class="margin-rail" aria-label="Links to Dean">
      <div class="margin-note"><span class="margin-note__label">GitHub</span><p><a href="https://github.com/loftwah" rel="me">github.com/loftwah ↗</a></p></div>
      <div class="margin-note"><span class="margin-note__label">X</span><p><a href="https://x.com/loftwah" rel="me">x.com/loftwah ↗</a></p></div>
      <div class="margin-note"><span class="margin-note__label">LinkedIn</span><p><a href="https://au.linkedin.com/in/deanlofts" rel="me">linkedin.com/in/deanlofts ↗</a></p></div>
      <div class="margin-note"><span class="margin-note__label">Get in touch</span><p>For work that fits the projects and practices here, contact Dean through X or GitHub.</p></div>
    </aside>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
